an absurd count must not turn a key walk into an exception

A capacity is a HINT and must not be able to raise. This sized an array from [self count], and a
receiver whose count is wrong turned a walk over the keys into an exception thrown from underneath
the caller: a constant dictionary reported 4317355096 entries and iTerm2 died on

    Please rethink the size of the capacity of the array you are creating

while setting a volatile defaults domain during launch. The enumeration does not depend on the
hint, so dropping it costs a few reallocations. A count that cannot be right is still REPORTED,
once, because a dictionary that miscounts is a defect of its own.

--- a/NSDictionary.m
+++ b/NSDictionary.m
@@ -794,10 +794,39 @@
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * A CAPACITY IS A HINT AND MUST NOT BE ABLE TO RAISE.
+ *
+ * This asked for an array sized by [self count], and a count that is wrong turns a walk over the
+ * keys into an exception thrown from underneath the caller. iTerm2 sets a volatile defaults domain
+ * while it launches, Foundation validates it with NSIsPlistType, that enumerates, and the walk died
+ * here on
+ *
+ *     Please rethink the size of the capacity of the array you are creating: 22387800
+ *
+ * with the real number larger still, since the message prints an NSUInteger through %d. The
+ * enumeration itself is unaffected by the hint, so dropping it costs a few reallocations and makes
+ * this correct for a receiver whose count cannot be trusted.
+ *
+ * The count is still REPORTED once when it is absurd, because a dictionary that miscounts is a
+ * defect of its own and this is the only place it has ever been seen.
+ */
+static void _CiderCheckDictionaryCount(id dictionary, NSUInteger count)
+{
+    static BOOL reported = NO;
+
+    if (count > (NSUInteger) 0x40000000 && !reported) {
+        reported = YES;
+        fprintf(stderr, "cider: dictionary of class %s reports a count of %llu\n",
+                object_getClassName(dictionary), (unsigned long long) count);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+}
+
 - (NSArray *)allKeys
 {
-    NSUInteger count = [self count];
-    NSMutableArray *keys = [[NSMutableArray alloc] initWithCapacity:count];
+    _CiderCheckDictionaryCount(self, [self count]);
+    NSMutableArray *keys = [[NSMutableArray alloc] init];
     NSEnumerator *enumerator = [self keyEnumerator];
     id key = nil;
 
